# test_report_mechanism.py was ignored here after CodeQL #193
# (py/clear-text-logging-sensitive-data) fired on its own result
# printer. The finding traced a loop variable literally named `secret`
# -- a canary string the test plants so it can prove the string is
# ABSENT from the report file. Renamed to `canary`, which is what it
# always was, and the file is tracked again: it is the 49-check guard
# for the reporting mechanism the Store rejected v2.16.1 over, and it
# belongs in every tree.

